  "Meet Kenta, the IGCSE student behind DevFoundy. A personal story about programming, independent projects, music, fitness, and building useful things.": "DevFoundyを運営するIGCSE学生Kentaの紹介。プログラミング、個人制作、音楽、運動、役立つものを作る歩み。",
  "My story — Kenta | DevFoundy": "私のストーリー — Kenta | DevFoundy",
  "Story navigation": "ストーリーナビゲーション",
  "My story / The person behind DevFoundy": "私のストーリー / DevFoundyを作る人",
  "I’m Kenta.": "Kentaです。",
  "A student with a passion for building.": "ものづくりが好きな学生。",
  "IGCSE student, programmer, and the person behind DevFoundy. Here’s a little more about me and the things I put my energy into.": "IGCSEを学ぶ学生で、プログラマー、そしてDevFoundyの運営者です。自分のことと、力を入れている活動を紹介します。",
  "Student": "学生",
  "A student, and always learning": "学生として、学び続ける",
  "I’m an IGCSE student with a passion for programming. Studying is one part of my life; building projects is another. DevFoundy is where I bring that creative side together and share what I’m working on.": "プログラミングが好きなIGCSE学生です。勉強とプロジェクト制作の両方に取り組んでいます。DevFoundyは創作をまとめ、制作中のものを共有する場所です。",
  "I’m still learning and figuring things out. My projects give me a practical way to explore ideas, work through problems, and create something I can actually use.": "まだ学び、試している途中です。プロジェクトを通じて、構想を探り、課題を解き、実際に使えるものを作っています。",
  "Why programming matters to me": "プログラミングが大切な理由",
  "What draws me to programming is the ability to turn an idea into something real. A thought can become an interface, a tool, or a whole project. I like having a way to explore a problem by building a possible answer.": "考えを現実にできることに惹かれます。思いつきが画面、道具、作品になります。解決案を作って課題を探れるところが好きです。",
  "That interest runs through my work. JARVIS explores what a personal assistant can be. StageWrite Studio brings together songwriting and software. KineticForm focuses on planning and tracking workouts. Midpoint tackles the everyday problem of finding a fair place for people to meet.": "JARVISはアシスタントの可能性、StageWrite Studioは作曲とソフト、KineticFormは運動計画と記録、Midpointは公平な待ち合わせ場所を扱います。",
  "They’re different projects, but each gives me a reason to learn something and put it into practice.": "違うプロジェクトですが、それぞれが学びと実践の理由になります。",
  "The interests behind the projects": "プロジェクトの背景にある興味",
  "My projects also reflect interests beyond code. Music and fitness both have a place in what I’m making, and I enjoy exploring how software can support those parts of life.": "音楽や運動も作品に表れています。ソフトで暮らしのそうした部分を支える方法を探るのが好きです。",
  "StageWrite Studio is the clearest connection between my interest in music and my programming work: a space to explore chords, arrangements, and songwriting ideas.": "StageWrite Studioは、音楽とプログラミングが最も直接つながる作品です。コード、編曲、作曲の構想を探る場所です。",
  "Fitness & progress": "運動と進歩",
  "KineticForm brings fitness into my project work, with tools for planning workouts, recording training, and looking back at progress.": "KineticFormでは、計画、記録、振り返りの道具を通じて、運動への関心を制作に取り入れています。",
  "Programming itself is a creative interest for me, too. Working on my own projects gives me room to experiment and decide what I want to make next.": "プログラミング自体も創作の関心です。自分の制作では、実験し、次に何を作るかを選べます。",
  "Building independently, and with others": "一人でも、人と一緒でも作る",
  "Alongside my personal projects, I build custom websites. It’s a way to take someone’s idea, business, or work and give it a place online.": "個人制作と並行し、オーダーメイドのサイトも作ります。人の構想、事業、活動にオンラインの場所を用意します。",
  "I also co-founded a tutoring website. That venture connects the education side of my life with my interest in creating things and working with others.": "学習支援サイトの共同創業にも参加しました。教育と、作ることや協働への関心がつながる活動です。",
  "DevFoundy brings those different threads together: student life, personal projects, custom website work, and an interest in making useful developer resources.": "DevFoundyには、学生生活、個人制作、依頼サイト、開発資料への関心が集まっています。",
  "What comes next": "これから",
  "I want to keep improving my projects, exploring new ideas, and sharing what I learn along the way. The DevFoundy journal is where I’ll write about that process, including the decisions, mistakes, and small discoveries behind the work.": "制作を改善し、新しい構想を探り、学びを共有したいです。ジャーナルでは、その判断、失敗、小さな発見も書いていきます。",
  "I’m still at the beginning of my story.": "私の歩みは、まだ始まったばかりです。",
  "For now, I’m learning, building, and seeing where the next idea takes me.": "今は学び、作り、次のアイデアの行き先を見ています。",
